+## POST-Gate Mode Bifurcation Table (`reflect_post_mode`)
+
+The `--cli` toggle bifurcates the POST-reflect gate into two mutually-exclusive modes driven
+by the single `reflect_post_mode` frontmatter key. This table is the one place that enumerates
+every divergence so a change to one arm is not silently missed in the other. Everything NOT
+listed here is SHARED (research fan-out, rf-* QA gates, the A.10.7 PRE gate, TCS computation,
+the instance-level anti-self-confirmation premise).
+
+| Field / Rule | CLI mode (`reflect_post_mode: cli`) | Skill-only mode (`reflect_post_mode: skill`, default) | Justification |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **POST item form** | FLAT `superclaude reflect run … --depth deep --fix --promote` Bash shell-out behind the `SUPERCLAUDE_REFLECT_WRAPPER_ACTIVE` skip guard (Rule 20 cli arm) | Dedicated-subagent runner invoking `/sc:reflect --mode post` via the Skill tool (Rule 20 skill arm) | CLI path is an executor-disjoint `claude --print` subprocess; skill path is an in-session subagent |
+| **`start_commit` frontmatter** | MUST be present (the wrapper's audit base when `--base` omitted) | MUST be absent | Only the wrapper resolves a base from frontmatter |
+| **`executor_model_class` frontmatter** | MUST be present (forwarded to reflect as `--executor-model`, accepted-and-ignored provenance) | MUST be absent | Only the wrapper forwards the compat flag |
+| **`--spec` at POST** | NOT threaded (wrapper audits via `start_commit`) | Threaded as `[--spec {SPEC_PATH}]` into the runner prompt | CLI wrapper takes no `--spec`; PRE gate consumes it in both modes |
+| **O4 POST depth floor** | Fixed `deep` (O4 forces Tier-2 fan-out) | TCS-derived, O4-floored at `standard` | CLI audits executed code (regression-escalation matters most); skill PRE has no diff yet |
+| **Validator clause (Rule 20 / §-checklist)** | Evaluate ONLY the wrapper-shell-out clause | Evaluate ONLY the dedicated-subagent-runner clause | Validator reads `reflect_post_mode` first; non-matching clause is SKIPPED, never failed |
+| **Validation status** | Session-validated end-to-end | **NOT yet session-validated** (see Rule 20 disclosure; prefer `--cli`) | Only the wrapper path has an end-to-end validation run |
+
+**Key-presence validation rule (referenced by the Task File Validation Checklist):** a generated
+tasklist with `reflect_post_mode: cli` MUST carry BOTH `start_commit` AND `executor_model_class`
+in frontmatter; a tasklist with `reflect_post_mode: skill` MUST carry NEITHER. A hybrid (cli mode
+missing a key, or skill mode emitting either key) is a MALFORMED output.
+
+---
+
 ## Reflect Depth (Deterministic TCS)

 The PRE reflect gate (A.10.7) and the templated POST item both derive reflect's `--depth` from a **Tasklist Complexity Score (TCS)**: a pure-arithmetic score computed from observable signals on the finished MDTM file + BUILD_REQUEST + spec. No inference is used except a single bounded tiebreaker within +/-4 TCS of a band edge (see below). Each signal carries a **frozen extraction rule (FER)** so two implementers compute the same integer from the same inputs.
